{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"57858470c12b0bd64ded781ee984991feab1bcaf922a929c0b33238484aeef14","packTokens":2273,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":208,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":790,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1169,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using authorized Folio3 Google accounts and have employee and vehicle profiles populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking and schedule releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can receive notifications and claim available spaces first-come, first-served.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record verification attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and automatically email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who receives a push notification when a space becomes available, and what should happen if delivery fails or a recipient has notifications disabled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Notify all eligible employees without dedicated parking; availability remains claimable in the app even if a push notification is not delivered.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What exact actions may Parking Administrators perform, especially when a holder's release has already been claimed and requires administrator intervention?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Manage employee and parking records, configuration, and reports; also reverse a claimed release when needed, recording the intervention.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What application access, if any, does a Security Guard need for entrance verification and recording entry status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Provide a guard-facing view of verification results and a way to record whether the vehicle entered.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Can an employee without dedicated parking claim more than one temporary space for the same date, and can they cancel or relinquish a claim before entry?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow at most one claim per employee per date, with no user cancellation after a successful claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should daily/weekly utilization and the overall utilization percentage be calculated, including the denominator and the treatment of released but unclaimed spaces?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Define utilization as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces for each reporting period; report released and claimed totals separately and exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"May employees add, update, or deactivate their registered vehicle details after first-time setup, or must changes be made by an administrator?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Employees can manage their own vehicle records; administrators can also manage them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"When a claimant has multiple registered vehicles, which plate should be authorized for that temporary parking claim?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require the employee to select one registered vehicle when claiming; authorize only that plate for the claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How will entry events for stickered dedicated vehicles be captured for utilization, given that those vehicles bypass system verification?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Have the LPR system record their plate-entry events without requiring authorization verification.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Require successful Google authentication with a verified corporate email matching an active directory employee before granting an employee session; refresh employee profiles and parking assignments from current source records, and deny dashboard access with recovery guidance when a profile is unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Populate refreshed profiles with employee identity, dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle details; require employees without a plate to register one before vehicle-dependent parking actions, while returning employees without a plate may view the dashboard with a registration prompt.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Allow employees to manage only their own vehicle records and Parking Administrators to manage employee vehicle records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Treat dedicated spaces as reserved on operating days unless released; let holders release today’s space with one action, schedule operating-day releases up to 30 calendar dates ahead, and make releases claimable at the configured time or immediately if released at or after that time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Allow holders to cancel unclaimed releases; require Parking Administrators to reverse claimed releases, revoke the claimant’s authorization for that date, and record the intervention.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Notify eligible employees without dedicated parking when spaces become available, while keeping spaces claimable in the application if notifications are disabled or delivery fails; allocate each space to the first successfully committed eligible claim, reject competing or duplicate claims, and show the current available-space count.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Require a claimant to select one registered vehicle, authorize only that vehicle’s plate, and return the assigned parking floor; do not allow employees to cancel or relinquish successful temporary claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Parking Administrators to manage employee and parking records, operating-day calendars, release-time settings, report settings, and stakeholder email addresses, and restrict administrative management actions to authenticated Parking Administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Ignore pedestrian and non-car detections; record permanent-sticker vehicle plate entries without authorization verification; and for other vehicles, normalize plate case and permitted spacing, require an exact match to a current-day temporary authorization, and activate the green indicator only on a match.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Fail closed when a plate is unreadable or the camera, indicator, connection, or authorization service is unavailable; keep the green indicator inactive, alert security for service failures, and record failures when service is restored.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Record each entrance verification attempt’s timestamp, available plate, verification result, and entry status, and allow only authenticated Security Guards to view results and record entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"At reporting-period close, record unused dedicated parking when the holder neither released nor used the space and unused temporary parking when the claimant’s registered vehicle did not enter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate utilization as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces, report released and claimed totals separately, exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts, and provide daily and weekly values with the capacity denominator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"At the configured Monday report time in the office’s local timezone, generate and email the weekly utilization report to configured stakeholders, including unused-parking records, daily and weekly utilization, released totals, temporary-claim totals, and utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Provide Parking Administrators with filtered on-screen parking reports and CSV export, and do not apply automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on utilization records.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}